\f0\b \cf2 \cb3 ## Undocumented use of a 3rd Party / external service
\f1\b0 \cb1 \
\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb3 Plugins are permitted to require the\'a0
\f0\b use of third party/external services
\f1\b0 \'a0as long as they are\'a0
\f0\b clearly documented
\f1\b0 .\cb1 \
\
\cb3 When your plugin reach out to external services, you must disclose it. This is true even if you are the one providing that service.\cb1 \
\
\cb3 You are required to document it in a clear and plain language, so users are aware of:\'a0
\f0\b what data is sent, why, where and under which conditions
\f1\b0 .\cb1 \
\
\cb3 To do this, you must update your readme file to\'a0
\f0\b clearly explain that your plugin relies on third party/external services
\f1\b0 , and include\'a0
\f0\b at least the following information
\f1\b0 \'a0for each third party/external service that this plugin uses:\cb1 \
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
