\f0\b \cf2 \cb3 ## Data Must be Sanitized, Escaped, and Validated
\f1\b0 \cb1 \
\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb3 When you include POST/GET/REQUEST/FILE calls in your plugin, it's important to sanitize, validate, and escape them. The goal here is to prevent a user from accidentally sending trash data through the system, as well as protecting them from potential security issues.\cb1 \
\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf2 \cb3 SANITIZE:
\f1\b0 \'a0Data that is input (either by a user or automatically) must be sanitized as soon as possible. This lessens the possibility of XSS vulnerabilities and MITM attacks where posted data is subverted.\cb1 \
\

\f0\b \cb3 VALIDATE:
\f1\b0 \'a0All data should be validated, no matter what. Even when you sanitize, remember that you don\'92t want someone putting in \'91dog\'92 when the only valid values are numbers.\cb1 \
\

\f0\b \cb3 ESCAPE:
\f1\b0 \'a0Data that is output must be escaped properly when it is echo'd, so it can't hijack admin screens. There are many esc_*() functions you can use to make sure you don't show people the wrong data.\cb1 \
\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb3 To help you with this, WordPress comes with a number of sanitization and escaping functions. You can read about those here:\cb1 \
\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls5\ilvl0\cf4 \cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://developer.wordpress.org/apis/security/sanitizing/"}}{\fldrslt \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\ul \outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec4 https://developer.wordpress.org/apis/security/sanitizing/}}\cf2 \cb1 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 \
\ls5\ilvl0\cf4 \cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://developer.wordpress.org/apis/security/escaping/"}}{\fldrslt \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\ul \outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec4 https://developer.wordpress.org/apis/security/escaping/}}\cf2 \cb1 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb3 Remember: You must use the most appropriate functions for the context. If you\'92re sanitizing email, use\'a0sanitize_email()\'a0, if you\'92re outputting HTML, use\'a0wp_kses_post()\'a0, and so on.\cb1 \
\
\cb3 An easy mantra here is this:\cb1 \
\
\cb3 Sanitize\'a0
\f2\i early
\f1\i0 \cb1 \
\cb3 Escape\'a0
\f2\i Late
\f1\i0 \cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f2\i \cf2 \cb3 Always
\f1\i0 \'a0Validate\cb1 \
\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb3 Clean everything, check everything, escape everything, and never trust the users to always have input sane data. After all, users come from all walks of life.\cb1 \
\
